    "&lt;p&gt;The use as noted above is not immune from enforcement action and is therefore unlawful under S.171B of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990 (as amended).&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:12pt;&quot;&gt;The applicant has failed to demonstrate, on the balance of probability, that the shipping contained and associated land at No 75 Vancouver Road has been used continuously as a B8 commercial storage use for a period exceeding ten years to the satisfaction of the LPA. As such, the development is not deemed to have met the threshold under section 191 of the Town and Country Planning Act.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;"
